<title>CHINA: China interbank market rates (CHIBOR) most down.</title>
<headline>China interbank market rates (CHIBOR) most down.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-12-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is the China Interbank Offered Rate (CHIBOR) for Friday issued by the official Xinhua news agency on behalf of the People's Bank of China, the central bank.</p>
<p>The figures represent weighted averages and not closing prices and are annual percentage rates.</p>
<p>		 1DAY   7DAY  20DAY  30DAY  60DAY  90DAY  120DAY</p>
<p> FRIDAY    11.160 11.709 11.488 11.398 11.399 11.987 12.193</p>
<p> THURSDAY  11.260 11.885 11.590 11.468 11.652 11.840 no trade</p>
<p>Volume surged to 6.7 billion yuan from 1.2 billion yuan on Thursday, with the 20-day contract the most active.</p>
</text>
